{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "qa-agent-api-collection",
    "name": "QA Agent API",
    "description": "QA Agent — auth, projects, ingest, multi-agent ask, documents.\n\n## Auth (Postman)\n1. Set `base_url` (default http://127.0.0.1:8000).\n2. Run **1. Auth → Start OAuth** — copies `oauth_state` + `authorize_url`.\n3. Open `authorize_url` from the response in a browser and approve GitHub.\n4a. Easiest: copy `access_token` from the browser JSON into collection variable `token`.\n4b. Or set `oauth_code` from the redirect URL, then run **Callback** (auto-saves `token`).\n5. Run **Me** to verify.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "oauth_code",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "oauth_state",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "authorize_url",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/health",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["health"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Root",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": [""]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Start OAuth",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (j.state) pm.collectionVariables.set('oauth_state', j.state);",
                  "  if (j.authorize_url) pm.collectionVariables.set('authorize_url', j.authorize_url);",
                  "  console.log('Open authorize_url in browser:');",
                  "  console.log(j.authorize_url);",
                  "  pm.test('OAuth start ok', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(j.authorize_url).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(j.state).to.be.a('string');",
                  "  });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/github/start",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "github", "start"]
            },
            "description": "Returns authorize_url + state (no redirect). Auto-saves oauth_state and authorize_url. Open authorize_url in a browser next."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login redirect (browser)",
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/github",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "github"]
            },
            "description": "302 redirect to GitHub. Prefer **Start OAuth** for Postman, or open this URL in a browser."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Callback",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "  if (j.access_token) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('token', j.access_token);",
                  "    console.log('token saved to collection variable');",
                  "  }",
                  "  pm.test('Login callback ok', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(j.access_token).to.be.a('string');",
                  "    pm.expect(j.user).to.be.an('object');",
                  "  });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/github/callback?code={{oauth_code}}&state={{oauth_state}}",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "github", "callback"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "code",
                  "value": "{{oauth_code}}"
                },
                {
                  "key": "state",
                  "value": "{{oauth_state}}"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Exchange GitHub code for JWT.\n\n1. Run Start OAuth first.\n2. Open authorize_url in browser and approve.\n3. From the redirect URL, copy the `code` query param into collection variable `oauth_code` (state is already set).\n4. Send this request — Tests script saves `access_token` into `token`.\n\nNote: GitHub `code` is single-use. If the browser already loaded the callback successfully, copy `access_token` from the browser JSON into `token` instead."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Me",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Authenticated', function () {",
                  "  pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "  const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(j.login).to.be.a('string');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/auth/me",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["auth", "me"]
            },
            "description": "Verify Bearer {{token}} works."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Projects",
      "item": [
